{"id": "EUVD-2026-86933", "enisaUuid": "b30dd11c-b0a2-34e8-b8ab-fd35c4e8d72a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: mcast: fix RCU list diversion in ip6_mc_del1_src()\n\nWhen removing a source filter whose count reaches zero, ip6_mc_del1_src()\nunlinks psf from pmc->mca_sources. If the filter was previously active,\nthe code moved psf directly into pmc->mca_tomb by updating psf->sf_next.\n\nBecause pmc->mca_sources is traversed locklessly under RCU (e.g. by\nipv6_chk_mcast_addr()), mutating psf->sf_next before a grace period\nelapses diverts concurrent readers to the tombstone list. Consequently,\nreaders miss remaining active sources in pmc->mca_sources and improperly\nexamine deleted tombstone entries.\n\nFix this by allocating a new tombstone node for pmc->mca_tomb (as done\nin sf_setstate()) and retiring the original psf via kfree_rcu().", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:35:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:13:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3343cd7ec8706c221e52b782f386b9af14a928a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4352737297b262e8367675c19a7dc6a9f53c97af", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8d4fe5c13f5056faa6deb09a90e24a89f9ebfad4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5149c60c406595b56fda0c6e9aae7fd287f636aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/93b49239840b91313adbd77b8b52993eff2d08c1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98102", "GHSA-g228-xhf6-wqq6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a7b041a-39dd-3451-8796-668ad687fceb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}, {"id": "4b3ad460-7e1f-365a-a92f-1f6b42e8ced9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "4d20791b-5531-3a63-b82a-a30451c215b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b200e398953c237c86d32bf26d4cb2a96556a6f <93b49239840b91313adbd77b8b52993eff2d08c1"}, {"id": "776a37e0-116f-3915-a074-ddbc792d9539", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "894df497-99cc-3aaa-b2a8-c117053d79aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "8cc1c682-e7e1-3bf4-90f1-8422a0737140", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "97ec8027-cd43-3b44-9f14-92dab688ece3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b200e398953c237c86d32bf26d4cb2a96556a6f <8d4fe5c13f5056faa6deb09a90e24a89f9ebfad4"}, {"id": "99f27333-720b-38f0-95f3-3aca4b014c7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b200e398953c237c86d32bf26d4cb2a96556a6f <c3343cd7ec8706c221e52b782f386b9af14a928a"}, {"id": "9b62689d-49e7-3f9c-90e6-74e44cdc6b87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b200e398953c237c86d32bf26d4cb2a96556a6f <4352737297b262e8367675c19a7dc6a9f53c97af"}, {"id": "a62f7475-2e77-37cb-b754-df1d2aec8201", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.261 <5.11"}, {"id": "cfd880ca-20f2-3762-8602-95c75f5ef5f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "86c49119f0353f857cc08030ec9e4ebaab3d5a64"}, {"id": "d1ba2ae6-7b18-30fb-b959-909df551b9e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b200e398953c237c86d32bf26d4cb2a96556a6f <5149c60c406595b56fda0c6e9aae7fd287f636aa"}, {"id": "d9d445ba-43c1-3799-a1e5-2322039a2859", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "dc71695c-6f83-3e73-8478-ae3939eb77af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "862901a7-1a88-3e52-ac58-45902473f61c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}